1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:06,110
Meet Office Axe — a Windows desktop workspace for preparing student documents.

2
00:00:07,810 --> 00:00:09,847
Type or paste a list of names,

3
00:00:09,847 --> 00:00:13,243
and Office Axe creates a folder for every student.

4
00:00:13,243 --> 00:00:18,404
The live preview flags duplicates and invalid names before anything is made.

5
00:00:21,887 --> 00:00:27,002
Every file previews right inside the app — Word documents and PDFs alike.

6
00:00:30,420 --> 00:00:32,531
To rename, just start typing,

7
00:00:32,531 --> 00:00:36,535
and pick a ready-made English and Korean document name.

8
00:00:38,914 --> 00:00:41,892
Select Word files and convert them to PDF.

9
00:00:41,892 --> 00:00:45,649
The work runs in the background with a progress card,

10
00:00:45,649 --> 00:00:48,059
and the originals are always kept.

11
00:00:52,628 --> 00:00:58,182
Arrange pages visually. Delete a blank page — changed your mind?

12
00:00:58,182 --> 00:01:00,352
Control Z brings it back.

13
00:01:03,317 --> 00:01:07,479
Fix a sideways scan, drag the cover letter to the front,

14
00:01:07,479 --> 00:01:09,411
and save it as a new file.

15
00:01:14,815 --> 00:01:19,429
Office Axe. Student documents, sorted.

